    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can confirm the correct property from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the entry point and improve visibility at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Identify and designate a flat, open area on the property where emergency vehicles can turn around, and keep that area clear of equipment, vehicles, and debris at all times.\n• Keep the full width of the driveway clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and overhanging vegetation so emergency vehicles can travel its full length without obstruction.\n• Post the property address visibly at the driveway entrance rather than only at the residence, so responders do not have to travel the full length of the driveway before confirming they have the correct property.\n• Trim any vegetation along the driveway edges that narrows the travel width or reduces clearance for larger emergency vehicles.\n• Keep the area in front of the detached structure accessible so responders can reach it without repositioning vehicles.\n• Confirm that perimeter gates, if any are present along the driveway, can be opened quickly from the outside and are not secured with locks unfamiliar to responders.\n• Consider providing a Knox Box or coded gate access at the driveway entrance if any gate restricts emergency vehicle entry."
  },
