    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches and shrubs that overhang or touch the sides of the structure.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the structure.\n• Cut grass close to the structure and keep it short throughout the dry season.\n• Thin scattered shrubs near the structure to increase open space between individual plants.\n• Clear dead grass and plant material from the ground around the base of the structure.\n• Trim overhanging branches along the driveway so vehicles and emergency equipment can pass through without obstruction.\n• Cut back shrubs and tall grass growing along the driveway edges to keep the travel path clear.\n• Remove any dead or dry plant material that has accumulated along the driveway corridor.\n• Keep grass along the driveway mowed short to reduce dry material between plants and the travel surface."
